  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $15.5B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency issued 22,884 awards at an average award size of $679K, and obligations fell 27.0% year over year. Annual obligations have trended downward from $34.3B in FY21 to $15.5B in FY26. All figures are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial: fiscal year to date. Spending mixes services, research, construction, insurance, and pharmaceuticals. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $2.5B of FY2026 to date obligations, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $1.3B and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $1.3B. Research and development categories and health-related manufacturing also appear in the top ten. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the largest vendor at $750M, followed by MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $272M. The snapshot shows smaller current-year totals compared with prior full-year obligations and a concentration in IT, consulting, R&D, and healthcare-related suppliers.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Department of Health and Human Services contract spending changed in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $15.5B in FY2026 to date, and obligations fell 27.0% year over year. Annual obligations declined from $34.3B in FY21 through $21.3B in FY25 and into the current $15.5B level in FY26. All figures are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial: fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the top contract categories and who are the largest vendors in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest category at $2.5B, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $1.3B and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $1.3B. Research and Development in Biotechnology is $1.1B and Custom Computer Programming Services is $1.1B, with additional categories including pharmaceutical manufacturing at $548M and building construction at $653M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the largest vendor at $750M, followed by MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $272M."
      }
    ]
